# CMS And SEO Rules

- URL paths must be manually controllable to preserve old SEO URLs.
- Do not store a whole page as one HTML field. Pages are composed from typed blocks.
- PageBlock content can use JSONB, but each block type needs a DTO, validator, Twig partial, and future Vue editor component.
- Public rendering is Symfony + Twig SSR with minimal JavaScript.
- SEO is critical: title, description, h1, canonical, robots, OpenGraph, schema.org, breadcrumbs, sitemap, and redirects must be explicit.
- Drafts and service pages must not leak into sitemap or indexable public output.
- Preserve clean HTML, correct heading hierarchy, lazy images, alt text, and accessible markup.

## Forbidden Shortcuts

- No WordPress importer.
- No shortcode parser.
- No blind WordPress database mapping.
- No monolithic `Page` god entity.
- No broad EAV model unless a specific use case requires it.

